   "is_new": true,
   "source": {
    "label": "thm:pm:easy",
    "number": "Theorem 2",
    "quote": "Suppose \\cref{alg:nw2} is run on locally observable $G = (\\cL, \\Phi)$ with parameters $\\delta \\in (0,1)$ and $\\eta = \\frac{1}{V}\\sqrt{\\log(K/\\delta) / (nK)}$ and $\\gamma = VK \\eta$. Then with probability at least $1 - \\delta$ the regret is bounded by $R_n \\leq C_G \\sqrt{n \\log(e/\\delta)})$, where $C_G$ is a constant that depends on the game $G$"
   },
   "confidence": "high",
   "notes": "Main text also sketches E[R_n] = O(KV/eps_G sqrt(n log K)) for games without degenerate actions (informal, not recorded). Polynomial compute implied (stationary distribution computation)."
  },
